forgeVideo({"file": "12-brd.en.html-player.js", "lang": "en", "title": "The BRD, a new artefact of the forge", "section": "Advanced concepts", "name": "BRD: a new artefact from definition to first document", "date": "23. 10. 2026", "pace": [4.0, 8.0, 16.0], "duration": 858.3, "events": [{"k": "card", "title": "The BRD, a new artefact of the forge", "text": ["Real work, not a demo. One session of 23 October 2026, about two hours shown, from the question at 18:34 to the write at 20:15. The save to git after it and the first trial of the new artefact on a real project followed and are not in the video.", "This is a cut: the times are real, the lines verbatim and shortened. The second LLM that appears in the video is Gemini."], "dur": 11.125}, {"k": "card", "title": "What you will see", "text": ["Before a new artefact is made, Claude says what is prepared and what waits on a decision.", "The principal decides item by item, fast where he wants speed; every proposition ends with the verdict line.", "Claude says plainly what a standard supports and what is only a convention.", "What the forge cannot know from the chain is named as something the analyst brings from outside, and is never written from imagination.", "A second LLM reviews the new block as a critic, and its findings are walked like any critic's."], "dur": 13.125}, {"k": "scene", "no": 1, "time": "18:34", "title": "What is prepared", "caption": [["Now", "The principal wants to know what is already prepared for a new artefact, the BRD. Claude says what he will read, reads it and opens with the result: the material is nearly complete, the verdicts are missing."], ["Why", "A new artefact is not written on a hunch. First it is shown what the forge already has (a brief, research, sources, mechanisms) and what waits on the principal's decision."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "do me an analysis of everything we have prepared for creating the brd artefact", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 7.575}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I'll go through the brief brd, the thread THR.0360, the research on the BRD, the fork's bundle in a library of the company's standards, the skill /new-artefact and the skeleton of an artefact definition, and put together what is prepared and what is missing.", "n": 4, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 4.62}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the brief brd and its history", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the thread THR.0360 and the fork's bundle", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the three research notes on the BRD", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the skill /new-artefact and the definition skeleton", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The analysis is done. The result first: the material for the BRD artefact is almost all prepared, including a proposed definition in seven blocks and an outline of the template. What is missing is not material but your verdicts on the open points of the brief and their mining into the intent. Only then can /new-artefact brd run.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "What is prepared", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The brief brd 0.2 (draft): what you want (start from the fork's BRD, verify against the standards, improve), a table of IDs, six open points.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The thread on the layer with an outside audience (THR.0360), closed 2026-10-22: a report for a third party is a work product, the layer below the intent for a handover is the BRD.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Three research notes:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the fork against intent 4.0: ideas to take over and anti-patterns;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the fork against today's engine: seven blocks of a definition, an outline of the template;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- what a BRD contains by the standards: ISO 29148, BABOK, IREB, INCOSE.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Sources: the fork's bundle in a library of the company's standards (template, skills, three BRDs, three critiques).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Mechanisms of the engine: the command /new-artefact, the skeleton of an artefact definition.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Candidate for a first real run: a company project, its assignment and beside it the fork's BRD as a comparison.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "What is missing or waits on a decision", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "| What                                       | State", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| Verdicts on IDs: BR, UC, DEP; REF; NFR     | open, proposed", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| Five remaining open points of the brief    | open", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| Mining the brief into the intent           | not done", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| Definition states/brd.md, templates/brd.md | nothing born, all has", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|                                            | ground in the research", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "The natural path: a walkthrough of the open points of the brief and the questions on IDs, writing brief 0.3, mining into the intent, then /new-artefact brd and a first /forge brd on a company project.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do you want to start with a walkthrough of the open points of the brief, the first being taking over the IDs BR, UC and DEP?", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 2, "time": "18:39", "title": "The IDs as a whole and what the standards say", "caption": [["Now", "The principal wants to speed up: try making a BRD as soon as possible and see the IDs as a whole. Claude gives one item with all seven IDs; the principal asks what the standards say about them."], ["Why", "Claude separates what a standard supports from what is only the forge's notation, and says what his knowledge rests on: secondary pages, not the paid originals."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "i need to speed this up a bit. let's rather go the way of trying brd creation on something asap, we don't have to think it through in detail. first the IDs, all the ones you want to use for brd. which we have, which are new, always explain the abbreviation too", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood, we go fast: try making a BRD as soon as possible, the details later in real work.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Item 1 of several: the set of IDs for the BRD. I propose it as a whole:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "| ID  | Short for            | Forge today| What it marks in the BRD", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| BR  | business requirement | new        | one business requirement:", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | one sentence, testable,", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | cites a REQ of the", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | assignment; qualities are", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | BRs too, in a group of their", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | own, no special number range", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| UC  | use case             | new        | a use case at user-goal", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | level: actor, preconditions,", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | outcome, main scenario in", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | steps, exceptions", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| DEP | dependency           | new        | a dependency on another", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | system, project or document", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| OOS | out of scope         | exists     | what is not done", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| ASM | assumption           | exists     | what the requirements rest", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | on and what would change", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | them", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| TBC | to be confirmed      | exists     | an open question with an", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | owner; whether it blocks the", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | estimate", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "| SCR | success criterion    | exists     | how the stakeholders know", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "|     |                      |            | the ask was met", "n": 1, "pre": true}, {"t": "REQ (requirement of the assignment) is only cited in the BRD, as the parent of a BR or a UC; the matrix REQ → BR/UC is generated from the items.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "What I do not take from the fork: REF (reference to a related document). The forge cites by file path and a link inside an item is forbidden. Nor the 0900 range for NFRs: groups in the forge start at the next hundred on their own, a special range would be a second mechanism for the same thing.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "My recommendation: accept as is, three new prefixes, four taken over, REF dropped.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "q what do the standards say about it?", "typing": 1.85, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The standards say nothing about prefixes; that is purely our notation. What they say about the things the IDs mark (verified on secondary pages, the primary texts of ISO 29148, BABOK, IREB and INCOSE are paid and I have not read them directly):", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The requirement as an item (BR): all four standards agree, one sentence, unambiguous, verifiable, traceable, uniquely numbered. Our BR meets that.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Use case (UC): no standard requires it. The form is Cockburn's and the consensus in practice; the UC is our addition after the fork.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Dependencies and assumptions (DEP, ASM): the standards do not tell them apart by prefix, but they do tell apart three different questions.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Related documents (REF): that is a list, not requirements; hence no ID.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "In short: the standards support BR, ASM, TBC, SCR and traceability directly; UC and DEP go beyond the standards but agree with them; REF and the 0900 range have no ground in the standards.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 3, "time": "18:47", "title": "NFR yes, FR no", "caption": [["Now", "The principal asks what the 900 range is, and does not want the type of a requirement read off its number. Claude offers two ways and recommends a prefix of its own, NFR; asked about FR, he recommends not introducing it."], ["Why", "Every option comes with a recommendation and its reason, stated once. The principal decides, with one letter."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "q what is the 900 range", "typing": 1.1500000000000001, "hold": 6.8}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The 0900 range is a convention of the fork: non-functional requirements got the numbers BR.0900, BR.0910 and on, a reserved block, so that they stood apart from the functional BRs at a glance.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "In the forge we do not need it: every new group starts at the next hundred on its own. A reserved number 900 would be a second rule for the same thing and with more than nine groups it would collide with them.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 8.425}, {"k": "type", "text": "imo that's nfr then, which we have? i don't want to tell br apart by type through a number range", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 1.5}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "We do not have NFR in the forge; the prefix does not exist. So the choice is between two ways of telling qualities apart, if not by a number range:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. BR in a group \"Qualities\". The type is given only by the group's heading; an item moved elsewhere loses the distinction.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. A prefix of its own, NFR (non-functional requirement). The type is in the ID itself, readable wherever the item is cited. The price: a fourth new prefix.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "I recommend NFR as a prefix. Your reason holds: you do not want the type in the numbers, and a group is weaker than a prefix, because groups can be rearranged and an ID is stable. The rules of an NFR are the same as of a BR: one sentence, testable, the value from the stakeholders or a TBC, never a number from the template.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 13.76}, {"k": "type", "text": "and will we tell fr apart too? br, nfr and fr?", "typing": 2.3000000000000003, "hold": 0.44999999999999973}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I recommend not telling FR apart. The reasons:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The group standard and the fork know only BR. FR as a layer of \"what the system does\" belongs by BABOK to the lower analysis, in the forge to the solution design or below it.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The border between BR and FR is blurred in a BRD. Two prefixes would force deciding the type of every item with no ground in the content.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- NFR is the one exception, because it has another form: a value, a condition, a population. Setting it apart is about content, not about type.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: new prefixes BR, UC, DEP, NFR; taken over OOS, ASM, TBC, SCR; REF and the 0900 range dropped, FR not introduced.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 12.605}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 4, "time": "18:50", "title": "Three ways in", "caption": [["Now", "Claude proposes the first trial on a company project, from its assignment. The principal asks whether a BRD could not also come from the intent or from any material at all, and then says how he wants to work."], ["Why", "The principal may change the procedure. Claude places his way of working within the forge's mechanisms (handing over, an automatic pass) and reworks the proposal instead of defending it."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted: the IDs for the BRD are BR, UC, DEP, NFR new; OOS, ASM, TBC, SCR taken over; REF, the 0900 range and FR not introduced.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Item 2: what we try the BRD on. I propose a company project, from its assignment 1.3 (draft; you say it is stable, and that is enough). The reason: the assignment is the most worked-out we have (109 REQs), and beside it lies the fork's BRD of the same project after three rounds of critique, so we have a comparison.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "q shouldn't the intent go into the brd along with the assignment? should it be possible to make a brd straight from the intent? or rather i give it any material (even a meeting transcript) and the elicitator tries to turn it into a brd?", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Three questions, three answers:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The intent goes in with the assignment, yes. The assignment carries the boundary but not the reasons; those stay in the intent.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. A BRD straight from the intent, yes. Where a project has no assignment, the BRD is derived from the positions of the intent by the same pass; the matrix then leads to POS instead of REQ.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. A BRD from any material: not directly, but by a short way yes. What someone said in a meeting never silently becomes the principal's position. The short way: the transcript is ingested, the intent is handed over to Claude from it, and the BRD comes from that.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 11.825}, {"k": "type", "text": "for me draft early. sometimes i need to take a quick look, pull a brd out of some document. draft early. ok, maybe the forge doesn't support it now, but we can change the forge. but let's build it so that it does it from the intent, the assignment (when there is one), or i can slip it something too. i just say, go ahead, in work run this file and push it through automatic elicitation with the brd skill and let's see what it shows. that's my modus operandi, what i'd want there", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I take it as a modification and build it that way. Your modus operandi fits the forge as a handover with an input of your choice, plus automatic elicitation: Claude walks the BRD map alone, writes what the material answers, leaves what it does not as a TBC or an ASM, asks nothing, and returns a draft with a short list of what he assumed. You look at what it showed.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "Item 2 reworked, three inputs of the BRD definition:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The assignment, read with the intent and the threads, when it exists. The matrix leads to REQ.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The intent alone, when there is no assignment. The matrix leads to POS.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. A file slipped in (a transcript, an offer, someone else's document, anything), ingested as a source and cited by path. The output is a BRD draft, into the chain, or as a work product in work/ when it is a quick look.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "In all three ways the same map runs in the same way: automatically on your word, or together in conversation.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "First trial: a company project, by way 1, automatically, and we see what it shows.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 6.975000000000002}, {"k": "scene", "no": 5, "time": "18:57", "title": "The fork is an inspiration", "caption": [["Now", "Claude proposes rewriting the fork into the forge's shape. The principal corrects him: the fork is not taken over, it is an inspiration, distilled by the standards. Claude rewords the item, after a short reply from the principal accepts it and gives the next item: who signs the BRD."], ["Why", "Modify is an ordinary verdict: Claude rewrites the item as the principal says and puts it again with the verdict line. The company's content lives in the library, the engine carries only a generic map."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted: three inputs of the BRD, automatically or together; first trial from the assignment, automatically.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Item 3: how the fork is taken over and where the company's content lives. Proposal: the fork is rewritten into the forge's shape (a definition in seven blocks, a template with items with IDs, no \"everything in tables\", no Version History in the body). The company's content stays in the library of the company's standards; the engine carries only a generic map.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "m the fork is not taken over. but it's the base of our inspiration. we're not dumbly forking, we want to make something good that matches best practice and the standards. and we distil something out of it", "typing": 3.5000000000000004, "hold": 7.405000000000001}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood, reworded:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Item 3, reworked: the fork is an inspiration, not a base to take over. The forge's BRD is built by best practice and the standards (ISO 29148, BABOK, IREB); from the fork we distil what held up in real work: the split of OOS, DEP, ASM, the use case with steps and exceptions, questions with an owner, mandatory testability, coverage of the touched areas with an explicit \"no\". What is not taken over does not get into the definition even in rewritten form (everything in tables, short assignments, company names in the engine, values from the template as requirements).", "n": 9, "pre": false}, {"t": "The company's content stays in the library; the engine carries a generic map.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Accepted: the fork is an inspiration, we distil by the standards, the company's content in the library.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Item 4: who signs the BRD. Proposal: the stakeholders' approval happens outside the forge, where the company does it today. The forge records only what it can: the principal's approval by a whole version number (1.0), and the Stakeholders section holds the roles and their involvement (approves, reviews, consulted, informed), no names.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 1.9149999999999998}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 6, "time": "19:04", "title": "The coding agent, and the brief written", "caption": [["Now", "The principal closes the last open point in one sentence. Claude sums up what brief 0.3 would carry, says it is only in the conversation so far, and asks about the write. After \"yes\" he writes the brief and its history and names the files."], ["Why", "One write at the end of the round, on the principal's word. What is not in a file is said to be \"nowhere\"; what is written has the name of its file and section."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Item 6: what the coding agent gets (THR.0670). Proposal: the BRD says what and why for the stakeholders and the estimate, the solution design says how; an agent that is to build gets the solution design, and the BRD with it as context. The thread THR.0670 stays open; in the brief the point stays with this view of mine, marked as mine.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "the coding agent gets the artefacts that will be available. it's a human's decision", "typing": 3.4999999999999996, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted with a change: the coding agent gets the artefacts that will be available; what they will be is a human's decision. That closes point 6 of the brief.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "That ends the round: all six open points of the brief have a verdict, and the IDs and the first trial are decided. What brief brd 0.3 would carry:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- What I want: the forge's BRD by the standards and best practice, the fork as an inspiration from which what held up is distilled; the company's content in the library.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- IDs: BR, UC, DEP, NFR new; OOS, ASM, TBC, SCR taken over; REF, the 0900 range and FR not.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Inputs and way: the assignment with the intent, the intent alone, or a file slipped in as a source; automatic elicitation on your word (draft early) or together; output into the chain or into work/.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Signing: outside the forge; the forge knows the principal's approval by version and the roles in the Stakeholders section.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Coding agent: gets the available artefacts, a human decides.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Report for a third party: closed as a work product (THR.0360).", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- First trial: a company project from assignment 1.3, automatically.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Still open: nothing of the original six; new only the document of the instance's roster, after the trial.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "So far all of this is only in the conversation, nowhere in a file. Shall I write brief 0.3 (the file projects/forge/00-brief-brd.md and the records in its history)?", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "yes", "typing": 0.15000000000000002, "hold": 7.032500000000001}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the brief's definition and the rules of the write", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: writes projects/forge/00-brief-brd.md 0.3 and its history", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Written:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/00-brief-brd.md 0.3: sections What I want, How a BRD is started, The IDs, Decided, Still open, The material.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/00-brief-brd.history.md: one record 0.3 with the wording that ceased to hold (Was).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Ledger regenerated; the brief stands as 0.3, draft, mining pending.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The next step is mining the brief into the forge intent, then /new-artefact brd. I can do both as a handover: I propose the whole block at once, you judge the block as a whole.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do we run /forge intent forge now, like that, as a handover?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 7.2325}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 7, "time": "19:10", "title": "Build first, the intent after", "caption": [["Now", "The principal hands the definition over, but wants to build and try first, the intent and the design only after. Claude shows the forge's position that allows it, proposes three files and, on two questions, explains the three kinds of reviewers."], ["Why", "A change to the operating layer may go in the order brief, build, trial, intent; until then the brief is the authority. Every reviewer has one job: the check the conventions, the critic the quality of the document, the challenger the substance."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "i'll hand it over to you. but i'm rather thinking - shouldn't we first make the agent and the critic, try it a couple of times, tune it and then write the intent and the sd from that? so we don't rewrite the intent here 15 times. i'll tell you later how we'll try it", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the history of the position POS.1780", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I agree, and the forge already allows it: the position on the order of a change to the operating layer (POS.1780, decided today) says exactly this: the brief first in your words (we have 0.3), then the build and its trial, then right away the rounds of the intent and the design. Until then the brief is the authority.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "What I would build for the trial, as a handover, the whole block at once:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Definition .claude/skills/forge/states/brd.md: seven blocks from the research, adjusted by today's verdicts.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. Template templates/brd.md: fifteen sections, items with IDs, no value in the skeleton.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. Check .claude/agents/check-brd.md: the mechanics of the matrix, IDs, terms, phasing.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "The birth of three files is a step on your word. Shall I write them?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "is architect also a check?", "typing": 1.3, "hold": 4.982499999999999}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "No. Architect is a challenger persona, not a check. Three kinds of reviewers in the forge:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- A check verifies mechanical conformance with the conventions: IDs, headers, indexes, matrices. We have engine, light, project, history, single-source-of-truth. The proposed check-brd would be this kind.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- A critic (lens) judges the quality of a document, not its content: clarity (unambiguity, requirement style) and essence (drift between layers). No new one for the BRD, both lenses read it with the rules from the definition.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- A challenger (persona) attacks the substance of the thinking: cto (assumptions, blind spots, organisational reality) and architect (how what is wanted is realised, the price of the choices, what breaks first). For the BRD the persona business-analyst would come into question; the research recommends waiting until the first BRD shows whether it hunts anything other than cto.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "The fork's critic did all three jobs at once; in the forge it splits into three places and the only new file is the check.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "So shall I write those three files?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "do we have a check for sd?", "typing": 1.3, "hold": 0.9850000000000001}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "No. The solution design has no check of its own; its structure and IDs are watched by check-project. The same holds for the BRD: a check-brd of its own would add only the traceability matrix and the rules for the BRD alone. For speed I propose not building the check now and leaving it to what the trial shows.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Reworked proposal: write two files, the definition states/brd.md and the template templates/brd.md. Shall I write them?", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 6.615}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 8, "time": "19:14", "title": "What comes from outside", "caption": [["Now", "The principal wants the challenger business-analyst too, and one more thing: the forge is to remind the analyst what he must supply from outside. Claude lays it out in four places, the principal adds NFRs without values, and Claude writes four files as one block."], ["Why", "What the forge cannot know from the intent or the assignment is named as a dependency or an open question with an owner, never written from imagination. The value of a quality is the stakeholders' to give; Claude proposes none."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "probably yes, but i want a challenger business analyst too, the same as architect. let the check do the checking. somewhere in the elicitation, the check or the brd challenger it should be: a lot of things can't be read out of the intent or even the assignment. it's on the analyst to tie it to the supplier documentation, a billion other standards. we don't do and don't plan to do architecture in the forge. so that it reminds him of the things it doesn't have and he must supply from outside", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood, and it is an important trait: the forge cannot and will not do what the analyst does from outside, that is tying the BRD to supplier documentation, systems documentation, standards and regulation. It is to remind him of it. I'll work it into four places:", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Definition, the map: an area \"what comes from outside\": what the BRD needs and neither the intent nor the assignment carries; supplier and systems documentation, standards, regulation; each such thing named as a DEP or a TBC with an owner, never written from imagination. Partner: Claude fills in only from what is in front of him; what must come from outside he lists as what the analyst must supply.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Template: a section for those dependencies and questions, where the list \"supply from outside\" stands visibly.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Challenger business-analyst (from the persona skeleton, the same as architect): hunts for what was written from the intent though it belongs to supplier or systems documentation; a standard or regulation that applies and is not cited; a use case that bypasses an existing process; a value nobody gave; an impact on a touched area that the BRD silently left out.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Check brd: the matrix (every REQ of the parent mapped, every cited ID existing), an item with no parent and no source, phasing present, terms defined, IDs in tens, no link inside an item.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Four files in all: definition, template, challenger, check. I'll write them all at once as a handover and you judge the block as a whole.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Shall I write them?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "yep agreed and it applies to nfr - which you can't propose. maybe sometime in the future we could make a list of typical nfrs the analyst must deliver (like availability, throughput etc etc.)", "typing": 3.4999999999999996, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Agreed. I'll put a list of typical NFR categories into the template right away: availability and continuity with RPO/RTO, performance, security and privacy, compliance, reliability, usability and accessibility, localisation, operability, compatibility, scalability, data integrity. In the skeleton each category will be a line with a TBC and no value; the analyst supplies the value from the stakeholders, Claude proposes none.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "Writing four files.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the model definition and template of the assignment", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the skeletons of a persona and a check", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: writes templates/brd.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: writes .claude/agents/challenger-business-analyst.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: writes .claude/agents/check-brd.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: .claude/skills/forge/states/brd.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Written, four new files of the operating layer, none of it in git yet:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/skills/forge/states/brd.md: a definition in seven blocks; three parents, an automatic pass on your word, a map area \"what comes from outside\" and, in the Partner block, explicitly what Claude does not write from imagination (values of qualities, behaviour of systems, rules of standards).", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "- templates/brd.md: sixteen sections, Qualities with eleven NFR categories without values, Open questions with a list \"To be supplied from outside\".", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/agents/challenger-business-analyst.md: the persona of a senior analyst, nine angles; the first is \"written from inside\".", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/agents/check-brd.md: five mechanical checks.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Judge the block as a whole; and then tell me how you want to try it.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 9, "time": "19:46", "title": "A second LLM as the critic", "caption": [["Now", "The principal wants the new block reviewed by a second LLM, Gemini, as a critic of the forge. Claude puts a package together and at first misunderstands who will send it; then, before launching, he states both steps and what leaves the machine, and waits for the word."], ["Why", "Launching a program and anything that goes to the network is a step on the principal's word: Claude says exactly what and why. The second LLM gets the same ask and the same report shape as the forge's own critic."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "make an output, wherever you put it: it's for the forge project plus the github link, now we're doing this, the ask is such and such, here's the implementation proposal, what do you think of it, and return it as our fnd. and send it to gemini. when it comes back, process it as if it were our critic", "typing": 3.4999999999999996, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: reads the shape of a critic's report", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: puts the package for Gemini together", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The package is ready in tmp/ (708 lines, outside git). Contents:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Context: what the forge is, the GitHub link, which files of the engine to read, three research notes by link.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. What we are doing now and in what order (brief, build, trial, only then the intent and the design).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. Brief 0.3 verbatim.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. to 7. The four files verbatim.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "8. The ask: two questions (quality of the documents, substance) and the exact shape of the answer after our critic: findings without IDs with severity and category, Location, Issue, Why it matters, Suggested fix; no invented facts, findings first, no praise.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "Send it to Gemini yourself; I am not launching anything. When the answer comes, paste it into the conversation; I'll turn it into a critic's report and we walk the findings.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Waiting for Gemini's answer.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "what do you mean you're not launching anything?", "typing": 2.35, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Sorry, I misunderstood: I take it that I am to send it.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 1.314999999999999}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: finds how Gemini is called from the command line", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "What I would launch, in two steps:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. A check, with no effect: the version and the list of models.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The consultation itself, in the background, output to a file in tmp/.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Network: Gemini may look at GitHub in its answer, as the package asks; nothing else leaves this machine but that package and your signed-in account.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Shall I launch both?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 4.5175}, {"k": "type", "text": "yeah launch both", "typing": 0.8, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "PowerShell: checks the version and the list of models", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "PowerShell: launches the Gemini consultation in the background", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Running in the background: Gemini is reading the package from tmp/. I'll let you know when it finishes; then I'll store the answer as a source and turn it into a critic's report.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 3.465}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 10, "time": "19:54", "title": "The second LLM's report", "caption": [["Now", "Gemini's answer is stored as a critic's report with ten findings. Claude says what he added to the text, sums up each finding in one sentence and, separately, marked as his own, gives a first impression. The principal wants to start with the contested findings."], ["Why", "The report of another model is stored word for word, and every change to it is said. Claude's view stands apart from the findings, so that the principal judges each on its own."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: turns Gemini's answer into a critic's report", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Stored as a critic's report: projects/forge/reviews/2026-10-23-critique-external-gemini-2153-337a.md findings FND.2530 to FND.2620, ledger regenerated. Gemini's text is word for word, only with IDs in the headings; I added one thing, the section Delta summary with the line New, which our shape has and Gemini did not return, because the ledger reads new findings from it.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "What Gemini found:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- high, contradiction (FND.2530): NFRs from the template's categories have no parent in the assignment, so every standard BRD fails the check \"every item cites a parent\".", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- high, inconsistency (FND.2540): a source as the BRD's parent bypasses the trunk of the chain and the rule that what was said in a meeting never silently becomes a position.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- high, contradiction (FND.2550): the automatic mode may neither invent nor ask, and the check forbids skeleton leftovers; so the owner of a TBC has no way to come about.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- high, duplication (FND.2560): the persona business-analyst does the work of the essence lens, the clarity lens and the check.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- medium, substance (FND.2570): the map and the template have no domain entities and their lifecycle.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- medium, contradiction (FND.2580): the check wants an item to \"end with its parent\", but a UC has its parent in the block's header.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- medium, inconsistency (FND.2590): a use case without a Trigger, Outcome merges the minimal and the success guarantee.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- medium, ambiguity (FND.2600): the Version column in the phasing is confused with the document's version, and the phases cite no item IDs.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- low, substance (FND.2610): the quality categories diverge from ISO 25010.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- low, ambiguity (FND.2620): the Stakeholders table has no Responsible role.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Recommendations outside the findings: shall only for BR and NFR, UC steps in the active voice; a \"generated\" matrix with no generator, say that Claude compiles it at the write; a project with no enterprise roster to have Roster: none.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "My first impression, as mine only: FND.2530, FND.2550 and FND.2580 are real contradictions in my four files and I'll gladly fix them; FND.2540 goes against your decision on the file slipped in, and that is your verdict, not his.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "Shall we walk the findings, from the heaviest?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "let's go from the contested ones", "typing": 1.6, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 11, "time": "20:07", "title": "A contested finding, and a boundary", "caption": [["Now", "First the most contested finding: a source as the BRD's parent. Claude shows where Gemini stands against the principal's decision and offers a compromise; on domain entities the principal then sets the boundary between the BRD and the solution design himself."], ["Why", "A finding of the second LLM is weighed like any critic's: it holds, holds in part, or goes against a decision that is the principal's. Where two layers meet, the principal says where the boundary runs."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I'll start with the most contested.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "A source as the BRD's parent bypasses the trunk of the chain (FND.2540, high). Gemini: only the assignment or the intent may be the BRD's parent; a transcript or an offer slipped in bypasses the intent, promotes others' statements to binding BRs and UCs, cites unstable places in someone else's file, and the brief itself says it wants a position in the intent. It proposes: a source either through /forge intent, or as a work product in work/, not as an artefact of the chain.", "n": 8, "pre": false}, {"t": "My view: it does go against the rule, but you decided it knowingly as your modus operandi and the definition says so. What stands in the finding: citing \"a place in the source\" is indeed fragile, but the source is immutable, so the place does not move. A compromise that keeps your modus and takes half of Gemini's: from a source the BRD always comes out as a draft in work/; into the chain as 30-brd.md only with the intent or the assignment as parent. If you then want it in the chain, the intent is handed over from the same source and the BRD is rewired to it.", "n": 9, "pre": false}, {"t": "I recommend modify to that compromise; reject is just as legitimate, it is your decision from today's round.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "i think when i slip it some junk, an artefact probably shouldn't come out of it by default. that the output goes to work is an ok compromise for me", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted as modify: from a source the BRD always comes out as a work product in work/, never as an artefact of the chain; the parent of 30-brd.md is only the assignment or the intent.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Domain entities and their lifecycle are missing (FND.2570, medium). Gemini: the map and the template jump from scope straight to use cases and requirements; without shared entities and states (an order: placed, paid, cancelled) the rules can be neither estimated nor verified. It proposes a section \"Domain entities and data concepts\".", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "My view: justified, and it is exactly what the analyst supplies from outside, from knowing the systems. But a separate section with attributes slides into a data model, that is into the solution design. I propose a map area for the entities and their states, and in the template an extension of Terms by a column \"States / lifecycle\". No attributes.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "I recommend modify like that.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "imo business analysis should say where from, which system they're taken from, but the sd then says the mechanics", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Agreed, that is exactly the boundary: the BRD says what it is, what states it tends to be in and which system it is taken from; the solution design says how it gets from there. Reworked proposal:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- map area: \"the things the business talks about: the entities, the states each may be in and what moves it between them, and the system each is taken from, as the business names them; how it is taken is the solution design's\";", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- template: Terms extended by the columns States and Source system, only for terms that are an entity; no attributes.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 11.09}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 12, "time": "20:13", "title": "The reflection and one write", "caption": [["Now", "All ten findings have a verdict. Before the write Claude shows what changes where, says none of it is in a file yet, and on the word \"write\" writes the whole round at once."], ["Why", "One write at the end of the round, after a reflection: the write confirms, it does not surprise. The report after the write names every file; git is the next step."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted. All ten findings have a verdict, none rejected. Before the write, a reflection of what changes:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Definition states/brd.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Inputs: the parent only the assignment or the intent; a file slipped in always to work/ (FND.2540).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Map: an area of entities with states and source system (FND.2570).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Course: the automatic mode gives owner: unassigned (FND.2550).", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Requirement style: an NFR cites a REQ or a category (FND.2530).", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Template templates/brd.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- parent: only two values; Stakeholders with responsible (FND.2620).", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- UC with Trigger, Success outcome, Minimal guarantee (FND.2590).", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Qualities: ten categories with Safety (FND.2610).", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Phasing with the columns Phase and Items carried (FND.2600).", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Terms with States and Source system.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Persona challenger-business-analyst.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Two angles out, a third narrowed to the silent category (FND.2560).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Check check-brd.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The UC's parent in the line Carries (FND.2580); owner: unassigned valid (FND.2550); a category as an NFR's parent (FND.2530).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Brief 00-brief-brd.md 0.4", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The third input always ends in work/; a record in the history.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Records of the findings", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- FND.2540 closed by brief version 0.4; the other nine by a record closed in the intent's history, with no version bump. Then the ledger.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "None of this is in a file yet. Shall I write it?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "type", "text": "write", "typing": 0.25, "hold": 7.25}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: the template, the persona and the check", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: .claude/skills/forge/states/brd.md, six edits", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: templates/brd.md, nine edits", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: .claude/agents/challenger-business-analyst.md, four edits", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: .claude/agents/check-brd.md, three edits", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Bash: writes brief 0.4 and the history records", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Written, all on disk, nothing in git:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/skills/forge/states/brd.md: Inputs, Map, Course, Requirement style.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- templates/brd.md: parent, Stakeholders, UC, Qualities, Phasing, Terms.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/agents/challenger-business-analyst.md: two angles out, \"The quality that is silent\" in place of \"The value nobody gave\".", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/agents/check-brd.md: the UC's parent, the NFR's parent, owner: unassigned.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/00-brief-brd.md 0.4 and its history.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/10-intent.history.md: records closed, the intent's version unchanged.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Ledger: all ten findings resolved, brief 0.4 draft, mining pending.", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 3.5125}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "card", "title": "What to take away", "text": ["Before a new artefact, Claude says what is prepared and what waits on the principal.", "Every item ends with the verdict line and nothing is written before his word.", "What the forge cannot know from the chain is named as something to supply from outside, never written from imagination.", "A second LLM's review is weighed item by item, like any critic's."], "dur": 9.625}]});
